#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166599 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "597e3939-e6b4-5237-a16e-8bae92f9b656" :knowledge-point/title "Basic Derivatives of the Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "3817c58a-1176-5347-aa96-2846969cae32" :question/math-academy-id "e-8349" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $y = 3\\sech{x}+\\coth{x}$." :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nFirst, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\sech x)' = -\\sech x\\tanh x, \\quad (\\csch x)' = -\\csch x \\coth x, \\quad (\\coth x)' = -\\csch^2 x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results and the rules of differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(3sech x + \\coth x) \\\\\n&= 3\\frac{d}{dx}(sech x) + \\frac{d}{dx}(\\coth x) \\\\\n&= 3(-sech x\\tanh x) + (-csch^{2} x) \\\\\n&=-3sech x\\tanh x - csch^{2} x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166600 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166762 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6fd03e86-fab7-5157-b0f3-62c522dc212c" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "b14f0558-456d-51a9-85ac-0b36158bc52e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8350" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) =\\coth(5x - 2)$." :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf =\\coth{g}, \\qquad g = 5x - 2\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}g} \\cdot \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}g} {\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}g} = -\\csch^2{g}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}g} {\\textrm{d}x} = 5\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{df}{dx} &= -csch^{2} g \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&=-5csch^{2} g \\\\\n&=-5csch^{2} (5x - 2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166601 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a991a2f4-b96a-5f92-8b52-6102647be98e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "4baa8799-f8ce-521e-833b-8b66c747e701" :question/math-academy-id "e-8351" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = x^2\\coth{x}$." :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nHere, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = x^2$ and\n\n$$\nv(x) = \\coth{x}\n$$\n\nSo, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= (x^{2})^{′} \\cdot \\coth x + x^{2} \\cdot (\\coth x)^{′} \\\\\n&= 2x \\cdot \\coth x + x^{2} \\cdot (-csch^{2} x) \\\\\n&= x(2\\coth x - xcsch^{2} x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166602 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08d9798e-a4bb-5f04-9d49-494990c52bff" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "bec9b472-31ce-5892-8a17-c4aa3c33ef12" :question/math-academy-id "e-8352" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = \\dfrac{\\sech{x}}{4x}$." :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\nu(x) = \\sech{x}\n$$\n\nand $v(x) = 4x$.\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= (u^{′}(x) \\cdot v(x) - u(x) \\cdot v^{′}(x))/([v(x)]^{2}) \\\\\n&= ((sech x)^{′} \\cdot (4x) - sech x \\cdot (4x)^{′})/((4x)^{2}) \\\\\n&= ((-sech x\\tanh x) \\cdot (4x) - sech x \\cdot 4)/(16x^{2}) \\\\\n&= - (4sech x(x\\tanh x + 1))/(16x^{2}) \\\\\n&= - (sech x(x\\tanh x + 1))/(4x^{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "597e3939-e6b4-5237-a16e-8bae92f9b656" :knowledge-point/title "Basic Derivatives of the Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8391f1f9-d35b-5902-a485-f98123940971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\coth x(csch x - 3\\coth x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165256} {:answer/id #uuid "01520480-6d4f-5062-a7fe-830d9b1ccb41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3csch x\\coth x - sech^{2} x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165257} {:answer/id #uuid "30b9fdf7-e53a-54db-8a2d-f58b6e4e3084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "csch x(csch x - 3\\coth x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165258} {:answer/id #uuid "477f0663-30e0-5c2f-8aca-c00fae809a23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "csch x\\coth x + 3csch^{2} x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165259} {:answer/id #uuid "7ea27e40-5cc1-5851-9429-b1ae0ce51aa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "csch x(3csch x + \\coth x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165260}] :answer-field/id #uuid "49a21963-b209-5ca1-abae-2d86c7c8ded5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165255}] :question/id #uuid "ea9f8f07-a38b-5320-8a01-10ad61981f4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-95282" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $y = 3csch x - \\coth x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a991a2f4-b96a-5f92-8b52-6102647be98e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fe2596c-add5-5ceb-a0d5-e04380d35f22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/m